==== what this decides ====
  MAXCAP 4096 (32768 B, the size 4 K context needs) : ACCEPTED AND RUN CORRECTLY - 4 K is blocked by something else
  over-limit cases: 2 declared above the limit, 2 had a pipeline created, 2 also round-tripped every element correctly
    (gfx803 has 64 KiB of LDS per CU, so an over-limit declaration CAN execute: the Vulkan
     limit is a software rule, not the silicon. That is why the engine may not rely on it,
     and why this is reported as the measured behaviour of THIS driver, not as a licence.)
  the engine keeps MAXCAP 2048 either way; the numbers above are what this machine did.
